# Research, design records, and working notes are personal artifacts:
# they inform the library but are not part of it, and they are not
# published. Their durable home is the state sink, outside every
# checkout (rules/visibility.md section 3).
research/

# Every dot-directory is ignored wholesale. Each re-admission below is
# one the product, the tests, or CI reads directly, named so that a new
# file lands ignored by default rather than published by accident.

# Runtime state only: run output, tool caches, and the legacy bin/ an
# install generates. Nothing here is tracked, so there is no re-admission
# to make -- a file that belongs to the library belongs in a tier
# ARCHITECTURE.md names, never here.
.orch/

# Project-scope skills ship to whoever clones; AGENTS.md names the
# super-research path, so validate's documented-path check reads it on
# a fresh clone. Designs and migration papers here stay unpublished.
.orchflows/*
!.orchflows/skills/

# Session-local host state, and the committed project-scope adapters
# that give a cloner the skills without installing first.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/skills/no/
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
.codex/

# CI is the repository's own gate: the workflows stay, nothing else here.
.github/*
!.github/workflows/

# Python bytecode, environments, test output, and tool caches.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
node_modules/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# OS and editor artifacts.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
